{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 16:13:33.662835", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Overview:\\nThe network consists of two hosts (`pc1` and `pc2`) and two routers (`router1` and `router2`) connected in a BGP topology. The connectivity between the devices is as follows:\\n- `router1:eth0` ↔ `router2:eth0`\\n- `router1:eth1` ↔ `pc1:eth0`\\n- `router2:eth1` ↔ `pc2:eth0`\\n\\n#### Observations:\\n1. **Ping Results:**\\n   - `pc1` to `pc2`: All packets failed with the error \"Destination Net Unreachable.\"\\n   - `pc2` to `pc1`: Similarly, all packets failed with the error \"Destination Net Unreachable.\"\\n\\n   This indicates that there is no end-to-end connectivity between the hosts.\\n\\n2. **Routing Table Retrieval:**\\n   - Attempts to retrieve the IP routing tables from `router1` and `router2` failed due to the absence of the `vtysh` command. This suggests that the FRR routing software may not be properly installed or configured on the routers.\\n\\n3. **Network Configuration:**\\n   - **Host `pc1`:**\\n     - IP Address: `195.11.14.2/24`\\n     - Default Gateway: `195.11.14.1` (connected to `router1:eth1`)\\n   - **Host `pc2`:**\\n     - IP Address: `200.1.1.2/24`\\n     - Default Gateway: `200.1.1.1` (connected to `router2:eth1`)\\n   - **Router `router1`:**\\n     - `eth0`: `193.10.11.1/24` (connected to `router2:eth0`)\\n     - `eth1`: `195.11.14.1/24` (connected to `pc1:eth0`)\\n     - Routing Table:\\n       - `193.10.11.0/24` via `eth0`\\n       - `195.11.14.0/24` via `eth1`\\n   - **Router `router2`:**\\n     - `eth0`: `193.10.11.2/24` (connected to `router1:eth0`)\\n     - `eth1`: `200.1.1.1/24` (connected to `pc2:eth0`)\\n     - Routing Table:\\n       - `193.10.11.0/24` via `eth0`\\n       - `200.1.1.0/24` via `eth1`\\n\\n#### Analysis:\\n- The network interfaces on all devices are up and configured correctly with IP addresses and subnet masks.\\n- The default gateways for `pc1` and `pc2` point to their respective routers, which is correct.\\n- The routers have static routes for their directly connected networks, but there is no evidence of BGP configuration or dynamic routing between `router1` and `router2`. This is likely the root cause of the connectivity issue.\\n- The absence of the `vtysh` command on the routers prevents further inspection of BGP configurations, which are critical for inter-router communication in this topology.\\n\\n#### Conclusion:\\nThe network is experiencing a complete lack of connectivity between `pc1` and `pc2`. The root cause appears to be the absence of BGP routing between `router1` and `router2`. Additionally, the FRR routing software on the routers may not be properly installed or operational, as indicated by the missing `vtysh` command.\\n\\nFurther investigation into the routers\\' BGP configurations and FRR software status is required to confirm and address the issue., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='d66117e1-1845-4cad-9906-bcd60f955205'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
